Fillets: a corner that PerformMoreSurfdata leaves undone fails the vertex
instead of corrupting the data structure (mitcad#121).

ChFi3d_Builder::PerformFilletOnVertex calls PerformMoreSurfdata for the
end of a stripe whose last surfdatas both meet the face at the end
(MoreSurfdata). PerformMoreSurfdata returns without doing anything where
those surfdatas are not as it expects (no common point on the arcs it
looks for, or the one on the arc not on an arc of the face at the end):
e.g. where the contact on one face leaves it near the end of the spine
and the walk there gave a surfdata with one side reduced to a point. The
stripe's end then has no points, ChFi3d_FilDS stores point 0 in the data
structure, and the topological build either throws
(TopOpeBRepDS_DataStructure::Point) or, without range checks, writes out
of bounds. The vertex now fails with an exception, as other corners that
cannot be computed do, and the fillet fails cleanly.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx
index 85f5818..00c95c2 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx
@@ -1618,6 +1618,14 @@ void ChFi3d_Builder::PerformFilletOnVertex(const int Index)
           if (MoreSurfdata(Index))
           {
             PerformMoreSurfdata(Index);
+            // PerformMoreSurfdata returns without a corner where the
+            // surfdatas at the end are not as it expects; the stripe's end
+            // then has no points, and the data structure built from it
+            // would refer to point 0.
+            if (stripe->IndexPoint(isfirst, 1) == 0 || stripe->IndexPoint(isfirst, 2) == 0)
+            {
+              throw Standard_Failure("PerformMoreSurfdata : corner not computed");
+            }
           }
           else
           {
